rfc791.txt, rfc815.txt, rfc1858.txt, rfc2474.txt, rfc3128.txt, rfc3168.txt, rfc6864.txt, rfc7126.txt
    The texts of RFC 791 (Internet Protocol), RFC 815 (IP Datagram Reassembly Algorithms), RFC 1858
    (Security Considerations for IP Fragment Filtering), RFC 2474 (Differentiated Services Field), RFC 3128
    (Protection Against a Variant of the Tiny Fragment Attack), RFC 3168 (Explicit Congestion Notification),
    RFC 6864 (Updated Specification of the IPv4 ID Field) and RFC 7126 (Recommendations on Filtering of IPv4
    Packets Containing IPv4 Options), downloaded from https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/ on 2026-10-26.
    License: the IETF Trust's Legal Provisions Relating to IETF Documents.
    Used: the rules the tests check (header layout and options of RFC 791 §3.1, fragmentation of §3.2);
    RFC 1122, whose §3.2.1 and §3.3.2 the tests also check, is in ../../arp/rfc1122.txt.

The IPv4 packets of the Linux kernel (fragmented echoes, Record Route options) are in
../../ethernet/linux.txt (see ../../ethernet/SOURCE).
